This project reimplements, for request-time use, the test-time image preprocessing and
camera-frame conventions of the following Apache-2.0 projects. One file is copied with attribution:
configs/bevdet-r50-cbgs-inference.py (BEVDet's model definition, used by the CPU smoke test).

- BEVDet (https://github.com/HuangJunJie2017/BEVDet), Copyright (c) Phigent Robotics.
  Conventions taken from mmdet3d/datasets/pipelines/loading.py (PrepareImageInputs, BEVAug)
  and mmdet3d/models/detectors/bevdet.py (BEVDet.prepare_inputs).
- MMCV (https://github.com/open-mmlab/mmcv), Copyright (c) OpenMMLab.
  Normalization order taken from mmcv/image/photometric.py (imnormalize).

Related to these projects:
- src/bevserve/model/cpu_ops.py is an independent pure-PyTorch implementation, written for this
  project and used only by the CPU smoke test. It computes the same forward result as BEVDet's
  bev_pool_v2 operation (mmdet3d/ops/bev_pool_v2, a CUDA kernel), using a scatter-add. It contains
  no code copied from BEVDet; only its call interface (argument names and order) matches
  bev_pool_v2, so that it can be substituted for it in tests.
- docker/patches/mmcv-1.7.2-torch27-get-stream.patch modifies one line of MMCV v1.7.2
  (mmcv/parallel/_functions.py), and is applied when building the container images.

No container image is distributed with this project. Images built from docker/ would contain
third-party software under its own terms (including NVIDIA CUDA/cuDNN base images and MMCV
operators listed in MMCV's LICENSES.md); those terms have not been reviewed for redistribution.

Data and model weights are NOT distributed with this project.

- nuScenes is provided by Motional under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 plus the nuScenes Terms of Use.
  Obtain it from https://www.nuscenes.org/ and comply with its terms.
- BEVDet checkpoints are published by their authors; obtain them from the BEVDet project.
  This repository contains no checkpoint files and no files derived from nuScenes.
